// ============================================================================
// CARLOS EMR - Health Tracker Flowsheet Decision Support
// ============================================================================
//
// Purpose:
//   Flowsheet-level rule base for the Health Tracker ("tracker") flowsheet.
//
// Why this file has no rules:
//   The Health Tracker is a scratch flowsheet whose measurement set is chosen
//   per provider/patient through Edit Flowsheet, so there is no fixed clinical
//   content to write timeliness or target rules against. Recommendations and
//   warnings the clinician configures are compiled separately from the
//   FlowSheetCustomization rows by MeasurementFlowSheet.loadRuleBase() (the
//   no-arg overload); this file only backs the flowsheet-level
//   ds_rules="tracker.drl" hook in healthTracker.xml.
//
//   The file is kept rather than dropping the ds_rules attribute so that
//   deployments can override it on disk via MEASUREMENT_DS_DIRECTORY -- that
//   lookup only happens for flowsheets that declare ds_rules, and site-specific
//   tracker rules were the original reason the attribute was there.
//
// Referenced By:
//   - XML config: healthTracker.xml (ds_rules="tracker.drl")
//   - Java: MeasurementFlowSheet.loadRuleBase(String) compiles this DRL
//
// Fact Class:
//   io.github.carlos_emr.carlos.encounter.oscarMeasurements.MeasurementInfo
//
// History:
//   - Originally created as an empty Drools 2.0/3.0 XML rule-set stub (McMaster)
//   - Converted to native DRL for the Drools 10 migration (2026). The legacy
//     XML rule-set syntax no longer compiles under the KIE executable model.
// ============================================================================
package TrackerFlowSheet;

import io.github.carlos_emr.carlos.encounter.oscarMeasurements.MeasurementInfo;
